                <li>The refund request must be made within 30 days of the initial purchase.</li>
                <li>Refunds apply only to software licenses and standard hardware purchases made directly from Vesopa EPOS.</li>
                <li>Hardware must be returned in its original condition, with all accessories and packaging included.</li>
                <li>Any damage or missing components may result in a partial refund or denial of the refund request.</li>
            </ul>
            
            <h2>3. Non-Refundable Items</h2>
            <p>The following items are not eligible for refunds:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Custom-developed software solutions tailored to your business needs.</li>
                <li>Installation, setup, and training fees.</li>
                <li>Subscription fees beyond the initial 30-day refund period.</li>
                <li>Hardware that has been damaged due to misuse or improper handling.</li>
            </ul>
            
            <h2>4. Refund Process</h2>
            <p>To initiate a refund request, please follow these steps:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Contact our support team at <a href="mailto:support@vesopa.com">support@vesopa.com</a> with your order details and reason for the refund request.</li>
                <li>If applicable, return any hardware components to our designated return address.</li>
                <li>Once we receive and verify your request, the refund will be processed within 7-10 business days.</li>
            </ul>
            
            <h2>5. Refunds of online card payments</h2>
            <p>Payments made online by card, Apple Pay or Google Pay through Dojo are refunded to the same card or wallet. A refund usually reaches your account within 3 to 5 working days of us making it.</p>
            <ul>
